@comment{
  Unpublished work (under review / in progress) carries `year = {WIP}`, which is
  deliberately not a number. jekyll-scholar groups the bibliography by year,
  sorts the group keys as strings in descending order, and renders the heading as
  the raw value (group_name -> value.to_s), so the label and the sort key are
  necessarily the same string. "W" (0x57) sorts above any digit, so the group
  lands ahead of every real year, which is what we want: work in progress is the
  newest. Do not add a leading space -- { WIP} sorts below "2" and would push the
  group to the bottom, after the oldest year.
}

